absolute path to stdout; add --json for the lease identity and metadata. All
banners go to stderr. A leased worktree is never handed out by a later get and
never removed by prune, even with no process running inside it, until you release
it with 'treehouse return <path>'.

Usage:
  treehouse get [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                  help for get
      --json                  Print lease allocation as JSON (requires --lease)
      --lease                 Durably lease a worktree without opening a subshell; print only its path to stdout
      --lease-holder string   Optional label recorded as the lease holder (defaults to $TREEHOUSE_LEASE_HOLDER)
      --no-fetch              Skip fetching origin before acquiring; use existing local refs

